# KFmt function documentation
This file explains in depth how the Killed Formatter (KFmt) works, how to modify it's code and norms that should be followed. It also covers the integrated language's syntax.
# Adding new functions
The general template for any function is
```zig
fn name(state: []const u8, par1: Type1, ...) ErrorSet![]const u8 {
    // ...
}
```
To make it indexable, you also have to add it to the index like this:
```zig
const transforms: []const Transform = &[_]Transform{ (... everything else), .init("public_name", @TypeOf(name), &name) };
```
where name refers to the function name, and public_name refers to the externally observed name.
# Input values
In the template above, Type# can not be a comptime type (like noreturn). It can only be an optional, a string, or an enum
